UID:93577-1788519600-1788894000@bangaloreinternationalcentre.org
SUMMARY:Expanding Agency and Archival Silences
DESCRIPTION:The travelling exhibition\, Expanding Agency: Women\, Race and the Dissemination of Modern Architecture\, offers a critical path towards reconsidering who is recognised in the making of architecture. By foregrounding women and racialised communities\, the travelling exhibition\, curated by architectural historian Kathleen James Chakraborty at the University of Dublin\, reveals how architecture is also shaped through education\, journalism\, advocacy\, patronage\, networks\, communication and other forms of professional and public engagement. Bringing this enquiry into the Indian context\, Expanding Agency and Archival Silences: Gender in the Built Environment\, invites us to ask whose contributions are recognised\, recorded\, ignored\, and what forms of practice remain outside conventional architectural histories. \nThus\, the Omitted from History Project (OMHI) delves into the questions of archival silences\, and the Women of Vaastukala Archive (WoVA) brings the lived experiences of women practitioners from across India into dialogue. Together\, with VIT School of Architecture’s panel discussion on journeys of diverse “women” architectural practitioners\, and PATIO Network’s critical take on “exhibiting architecture in South Asia”\, this collective of practices is creating a framework in which expanding agency is not simply about adding the omitted voices to an existing architectural history. It is about expanding the horizon of getting to know architecture; rethinking ways it can be encountered\, documented\, discussed and practised. \nRead more from the curatorial note here. \nExhibition Opening: 11am | Fri\, 4 Sep\nExhibition Timings: 11am – 7pm | Fri\, 4 Sep – Tue\, 8 Sep\nExhibition on Show Until: 7pm | Tue\, 8 Sep \nWalkthroughs:\n5pm | Fri\, 4 Sep\n4pm | Sat\, 5 Sep\n4:30pm | Sun\, 6 Sep \nGender in the Built Environment | 6:30pm – 8pm | Fri\, 4 Sep\nA panel discussion to launch the event\, discussing the exhibition and supporting programmes. \nHer Labour |  11:30am – 1:30pm | Sat\, 5 Sep\nThis roundtable public workshop explores how we can contribute to building awareness and solidarity with women construction workers\, across the barriers of gender and class. \nWomen Shaping Architecture in India | 11:30am – 1pm | Sun\, 6 Sep\nThis panel brings together practitioners to reflect on their professional journeys and the changing cultures of architectural practice.\n \nA Dialogue Beyond the Blueprints | 5pm – 7:30pm | Sun\, 6 Sep\nThis workshop explores the creation of a manifesto for feminist spatial pedagogies\, as a co-created framework that can critically transform how space and place-making are taught and practised\, both regionally and globally.\n \nLed by Professor Kathleen James-Chakraborty\, this project has received funding from the European Research Council (ERC) under the European Union’s Horizon 2020 research and innovation programme (Grant Agreement No. 101019419). \nView the full event schedule here. \nIn collaboration with:\n        \nVenue: Gallery\n\n\nGender in the Built Environment\nRSVP here (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdz9fwt-YWKkgFKBtoiSsrQu6sM3PgTxPsfOBpVYhejeq2zNg/viewform?usp=pp_url)\n*Curatorial Team*: Ishita Shah\, Meenakshi Jayan\, Sarah Melsens\n*Event Categories*: Architecture\, Environment\, Gender\, Media\, Visual Arts
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/expanding-agency-and-archival-silences/
LOCATION:Bangalore International Centre\, 7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bangalore\, Karnataka\, 560071\, India
CATEGORIES:Architecture,Environment,Gender,Media,Visual Arts
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Thumbnail-exh.png
END:VEVENT
