SUMMARY:Wearing the Landscape
DESCRIPTION:Should ecology take precedence over economy in today’s globalised design world? \nFrom seed saving and shepherding sheep to soil health and landfill\, this panel brings together voices who look beyond the label to the stories fashion doesn’t tell. Together\, they trace the journey of a garment from fibre to fit\, and ask why talking about fast fashion is no longer enough. \nEvery piece of clothing carries a hidden history — of land\, labour\, and the ecosystems it draws from. As consumers\, we are rarely invited to see that far back. This conversation makes the case that the back story of fashion deserves to be front of mind\, and that designers and consumers alike must look closely at the unseen stories behind what they consume. Only then can choices\, worn every day\, become informed ones. \nIn collaboration with: \n    \nVenue: Library\n\n\nTaking the Discussion Beyond Fast Fashion\nRSVP here (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdgsNCCCnM251rTgwTJ-ch_Ud0620aNV0jtKE4KrCpxFKCdHg/viewform?usp=publish-editor)\n*Speakers*: Anshu Arora\, Sushma Veerappa\, Nisha Subramaniam\, Jenny Pinto\n*Event Categories*: Environment\, Textiles
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/wearing-the-landscape/
LOCATION:Bangalore International Centre\, 7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bangalore\, Karnataka\, 560071\, India
CATEGORIES:Environment,Textiles
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Thumbnail-12.jpg
