SUMMARY:Women Shaping Architecture in India
DESCRIPTION:This panel brings together diverse practitioners to reflect on their professional journeys and the evolving roles as women in architecture. Extending the central idea of the exhibition\, the discussion intends to challenge the conventional perceptions about architectural practice in India by examining how women\, educators\, workers\, conservationists\, and other overlooked groups shape the built environment. \nThe conversation will focus on the lived experiences of practitioners: entering the profession\, establishing practices\, negotiating authority\, building leadership\, creating opportunities\, and responding to changing professional cultures. Gender is an important dimension of the discussion\, but not the sole lens through which the panellists are understood. The conversation seeks to recognise them as architects and practitioners while exploring moments when gender has influenced or shaped their professional experiences. \nThe discussion will also address professional identity\, gender and bias\, leadership\, mentorship\, collaboration\, recognition\, entrepreneurship\, and the changing culture of architectural practice. It will also consider what has changed for women entering architecture today and what challenges continue to persist. \nUltimately\, the panel asks: How have individual practitioners shaped not only architecture\, but the profession itself? \nThis event is a part of the “Expanding Agency and Archival Silences” exhibition. Find the BIC schedule here. \nView the complete list of events here. \nIn collaboration with:\n   \nVenue: Seminar Halls\n  \n\n\nJourneys and Leadership\nRSVP here (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfmKvC_wEADMaKYZrVh00JjkSzKzjcB6HBphAubtKGq9SkruA/viewform?usp=pp_url)\n*Speakers*: Ujjwala Khot-Palsuley\, Gita Balakrishnan\, Akshara Verma\, Radhika Desai\, Williams\n*Event Categories*: Architecture\, Gender\, Visual Arts
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/women-shaping-architecture-in-india/
LOCATION:Bangalore International Centre\, 7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bangalore\, Karnataka\, 560071\, India
CATEGORIES:Architecture,Gender,Visual Arts
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Thumbnail_DK-3.jpg
