SUMMARY:In the Language We Think\, Dream and Belong
DESCRIPTION:Every child has the right to read stories that are both familiar and new\, in a language they understand and call their own. This International Literacy Day\, this panel brings together three individuals working across the reading ecosystem to explore what it takes to make this a reality\, from creating books and empowering local voices\, to building the pathways that bring stories into children’s hands. \nAs part of One Day\, One Story (ODOS)\, Pratham Books’ nationwide celebration of India’s linguistic diversity\, the conversation will explore how stories in children’s own languages can help create a more inclusive culture of reading. What does it really take to enable all of India’s children to read\, and by extension\, to dream? \nThis session is part of a two-part event on enabling children to read. The first session\, “Let’s Fall in Love with Reading\,” is an interactive storytelling session for children. \nIn collaboration with: \n    \n\n\nBuilding a Reading Culture in Every Child’s Language\nRSVP here (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdFXsz_iSbfp1n2VEPONzMMMU2f3EpaiNWICNKlJtF5mf3V3w/viewform?usp=publish-editor)\n*Speakers*: Rohini Nilekani\, Nagakarthik M P\, Uma Mahadevan Dasgupta\, Parul Bajaj\n*Event Categories*: Children's Books\, Education\, Language
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/in-the-language-we-think-dream-and-belong-2/
LOCATION:Bangalore International Centre\, 7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bangalore\, Karnataka\, 560071\, India
CATEGORIES:Children's Books,Education,Language
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Thumbnail_ITLWTD...jpg
