SUMMARY:A Dialogue Beyond the Blueprints
DESCRIPTION:Can we relearn placemaking? \nThis workshop asks how questions of agency\, care\, resilience\, and regional context can be brought into architectural education and practice. The session begins with short presentations and reflections by members of the Feminist Spatial Practices network\, followed by presentations of invited practitioners from India. \nParticipants will then engage with project processes and experiences presented at the exhibition by the researchers of Women of Vaastukala Archive\, examining how feminist approaches emerge through practices of listening\, understanding\, and making different kinds of spaces. Working in smaller groups\, participants will collaboratively identify the questions\, principles\, and pedagogical approaches that arise from these experiences. This workshop explores the creation of a manifesto for feminist spatial pedagogies\, as a co-created framework that can critically transform how space and place-making are taught and practised\, both regionally and globally. \nThis event is a part of the “Expanding Agency and Archival Silences” exhibition. Find the BIC schedule here. \nView the complete list of events here. \nIn collaboration with:\n            \nVenue: Seminar Halls\n\n\nIn Search of Feminist Spatial Pedagogies\nRSVP here (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdyaYUZF7RT3t-vbT4-jPTyDncmIkKiYyH81bVVoCd5BSlOQw/viewform?usp=pp_url)\n*Speakers*: Renske Maria van Dam\, Mamuna Iqbal\, Lýdia Grešáková\, Abriannah Aiken\, Meeta Jain\, Gita Chadha\, Nisha Mathew Ghosh\, Shantesh Kelvekar\, Ishita Shah\, Meenakshi Jayan\n*Event Categories*: Architecture\, Gender\, Visual Arts\, Workshops
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/a-dialogue-beyond-the-blueprints/
LOCATION:Bangalore International Centre\, 7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bangalore\, Karnataka\, 560071\, India
CATEGORIES:Architecture,Gender,Visual Arts,Workshops
