UID:93356-1788892200-1788897600@bangaloreinternationalcentre.org
SUMMARY:Wow Kolkata
DESCRIPTION:\n\nThe Kolkata Restorers have one goal: to turn the historic\, forgotten buildings of the city into celebrated heritage through facade illumination. This conversation will explore how light\, restoration\, storytelling and citizen participation transformed Kolkata. \nIndian cities\, Kolkata in particular\, have architecture that carries the stories of generations. Many of these stories have gradually disappeared into darkness\, neglect and urban indifference. Facade illumination is a powerful instrument in the transformation. By lighting historic buildings\, domes\, columns\, arches and ornamentation\, architectural details that often remain under-visible by day are highlighted after sunset. What was once simply old becomes dramatic; what was overlooked becomes a landmark; what belonged to history becomes part of contemporary Kolkata. \nThis event is part of BIC’s Beyond the 9 to 5 conversation series\, featuring people pursuing ambitious\, unusual and meaningful projects outside their student and professional lives. \n\nVenue: Auditorium\n\n\nRestoring the “City of Joy” on a Tight Budget\nRSVP here (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSe4PSrFIC5Lr4fgV2GHwTdgSc2y-mBZQnRwVWO7_g6LYyesdg/viewform?usp=dialog)\n*Speakers*: Mudar Patherya\, Arun Pai\n*Event Categories*: Cities\, Development
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/wow-kolkata/
LOCATION:Bangalore International Centre\, 7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bangalore\, Karnataka\, 560071\, India
CATEGORIES:Cities,Development
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/ThumbnailWK.jpg
END:VEVENT
