SUMMARY:A Tale of Troubled Partners
DESCRIPTION:Relations between India and China have long been overshadowed by the boundary dispute. Based on the book CHINDIA: Journey to an Asian Century\, this session sheds light on the nuanced dynamics between the two Asian giants. Offering a contemporary chronicle of India-China relations and their trajectory between 2008 and 2025\, the discussion examines the influence of both domestic and bilateral factors. Can these two neighbours move past conflict toward the shared promise of an Asian Century? \nWhile acknowledging the setbacks dealt by Galwan Valley and other episodes\, the reasons that economic cooperation is essential to that march forward are made evident. Blending geopolitics with lived experience\, the session offers glimpses of Chinese society and politics\, comments on Indian diplomacy\, and comparisons of Asia’s two largest economies and populations. \nVenue: Gallery\n\n\nHow India and China See Each Other\nRSVP here (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLScEfEj5Rz6xU11XRJNTTnTaAhaqjhvx3n0-WBWLeCbJnDdlOQ/viewform?usp=publish-editor)\n*Speakers*: Shastri Ramachandaran\, Amit Kumar\n*Event Categories*: Books\, International Relations\, Politics
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/a-tale-of-troubled-partners/
LOCATION:Bangalore International Centre\, 7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bangalore\, Karnataka\, 560071\, India
CATEGORIES:Books,International Relations,Politics
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Thumbnail_ATOTP2.jpg
END:VEVENT
