SUMMARY:The Incidents at Pawgur\, 1830
DESCRIPTION:55 Mins| India | 2026 | English and Kannada with English Subtitles \nOur past is as mysterious and open to imagination as the skies above us. \nAmid the stark landscapes of Pavagada\, known to the British as Pawgur\, a fleeting UFO encounter draws in two researchers and a local explorer. They retrace the path of a 19th century British surveyor\, whose meticulous records of prehistoric sites lend weight to his testimony of witnessing strange lights at dusk in Pavagada. \nThe film blends documentary-style narration with fiction\, in a cinematic experiment that re-frames the UFO phenomenon through contemporary eyes\, situating it within a historical context where fact and imagination converge. \nVenue: Seminar Halls\n\n\nA Docufiction Journey across Prehistory\, Colonial Records and UFO Encounters\nFor Ages 15+\nRSVP here (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfRMuGkByFtMedbbrYiurZmTyno002ZvTvx_XsciRyYAJtc2Q/viewform?usp=pp_url)\n*Speakers*: Sashi Sivramkrishna\, RamG Vallath\n*Event Categories*: Fiction\, Film
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/the-incidents-at-pawgur-1830/
LOCATION:Bangalore International Centre\, 7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bangalore\, Karnataka\, 560071\, India
CATEGORIES:Fiction,Film
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Thumbnailalien.jpg
