SUMMARY:Vanapuri Vaathukaaran
DESCRIPTION:Language: Tamil with English subtitles \nEvery voice matters\, even more so the ones that are often unheard. \nUnfolding in a world nearing its end\, this play follows duck-header and clown\, Vaaththukkaaran\, as he delivers the last letters of humanity. Brought to him by a woman in a broken coracle\, letters carry voices silenced by war\, migration\, caste\, protest\, and loss. \nDrawing on the director’s experiences\, the work challenges long-standing hierarchies in theatre\, where power roles are reserved for dominant groups while clowns are reduced to caricatures. Here\, the clown is reimagined as perceptive and reflective\, reclaiming dignity and voice. Echoing B. R. Ambedkar\, the performance questions belonging\, identity\, and exclusion. \nSupported by: \n \n  \nVenue: Auditorium\n\n\nWhere Memory\, Migration\, and Identity Collide\nRSVP here (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdR19bidPoox1VbTMJq4dF2a6I-eCOfXpBV3eSDYSjQ2XJxLg/viewform?usp=publish-editor)\n*Performers*: Naren\, Sindhu\, Veeramani\, Arputhan\, Sachin Sreenath\, Reuben Paul\, Siddharth\n*Event Categories*: Performing Arts\, Theatre
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/vanapuri-vaathukaran/
LOCATION:Bangalore International Centre\, 7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bangalore\, Karnataka\, 560071\, India
CATEGORIES:Performing Arts,Theatre
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Thumbnailvv12.jpg
