SUMMARY:Read before You Sign
DESCRIPTION: \nFrom exploitative contracts to outright idea theft\, today’s economy is rife with pitfalls for independent creators. Based on the book Who Owns What?\, this discussion offers a basic understanding of the world around IP Law\, translating legalese into simple and straightforward concepts. \nMusicians\, writers\, filmmakers and other content creators often lack the knowledge and resources to protect their work effectively. Intellectual property lawyers can be prohibitively expensive\, and independent creators are often up against massive corporations with teams of legal experts-leading to the signing of highly one-sided contracts. This session aims to empower independent creators to advocate for themselves with confidence and clarity. \nIn collaboration with:\n \nVenue: Seminar Halls\n\n\nThe Essential Legal Guide for Independent Creators\nRSVP here (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSeR5vzj-WghHc974nvriBwL48lp8jU4PdJEuO5ml745lgeQ8w/viewform?usp=pp_url)\n*Speakers*: Xerxes Ranina\, Vishruti Bindal\, Sandhya Surendran\n*Event Categories*: Law
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/read-before-you-sign/
LOCATION:Bangalore International Centre\, 7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bangalore\, Karnataka\, 560071\, India
CATEGORIES:Law
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Thumbnail_RBYS.jpg
END:VEVENT
